From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 17:46:37 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(inbox): fail-closed targeting + actor parity + fenced
 list (review #379)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MAJOR-2 (wrong-agent leak): classifyClaim now keys on the CLAIM's discriminators —
a claim carrying session_id/worktree_id must be matched EXACTLY by the identity, else
no match; only a claim with both null falls to the actor floor. Prevents worktree A's
instruction leaking into session B when B's own worktree detection failed (both default
actor to 'forge'). Miss-not-leak by design.

MAJOR-1 (missed delivery): resolveIdentity derives actor via resolveIssueActor
(FORGE_ACTOR -> FORGE_SESSION_ID -> 'forge'), mirroring how claims are stamped, so a
FORGE_SESSION_ID-only session no longer rejects its own claims.

MINOR-1: forge inbox neutralize()s bodies/authors + fences the list block (dashboard-comment).
MINOR-2: documented board-ack broadcast semantics (per-issue ack). MINOR-3: documented that
the dashboard/serve WRITE path must create the dashboard-inbox chore issue (read path stays
side-effect free). NIT: exact ⟦END UNTRUSTED⟧ terminator fence-escape test added.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
